.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/promote-now-commit-on-branch.md:49:- `discussions/2026-05-24-promote-now-rollback-doc-home.md` — where the rollback semantics are documented (`preparation/SKILL.md`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/branch-prefix-sub-option.md:13:# Branch type prefix selection — chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/branch-prefix-sub-option.md:17:The initial worktree-first design draft used `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` as the worktree branch name. But `session/` is not in the registered branch-type registry (`feat|fix|hotfix|chore|docs|refactor|test|ci|perf|build|style`), so a branch named that way would fail registry validation and block CI/hooks. The branch prefix had to be corrected to a registered type.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/branch-prefix-sub-option.md:25:1. **`chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}`** — reuse the existing `chore` type from the registry; the `session-{date}-{ssid-short}` component satisfies the description-slug regex `[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/branch-prefix-sub-option.md:31:User selected option 1, `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` — use the existing `chore` type. `chore` is already registered, the description slug passes validation, and no registry extension is needed; `feat` was rejected because it implies a product feature.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/branch-prefix-sub-option.md:35:Design Decision D-1 and all branch-naming statements use `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}`. The registry-validation failure mode that would have blocked CI/hooks is eliminated.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:3:description: User confirmed worktree-first applies uniformly to every session, not only feature sessions; direct mode is the opt-out.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:26:2. **Uniform** — worktree-first applies to every session; non-feature sessions get a session-infrastructure branch with no issue prefix, and direct mode is the opt-out for the rare session that needs the main tree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/non-feature-session-scope.md:34:Every session boots on a worktree branch. The non-feature branch name `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` (no issue prefix) handles investigation and maintenance sessions. D-5 documents direct mode as the escape hatch for emergency hotfix or read-only sessions.
