.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/design/per-iteration-session-commit-cadence.md:18:Under worktree-first, the entire session directory lives in the worktree, and the worktree is removed at Wrap-up. Removal discards any uncommitted state, so session memory written during the session is lost on a mid-session abort unless it has been committed first. The open question was *when* to commit session memory to the worktree branch: once at Wrap-up, or at every iteration.
