+   - Reviewed discussion doc: `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/git-workflow/discussions/2026-05-24-direct-mode-opt-out-doc-home.md:19` and `:36` say `workflow.git.mode = 'direct'`.
+
+   Why this matters: this is not just provenance wording. The docs are meant to preserve the direct-mode opt-out contract, and a future agent could copy one of the two wrong spellings into instructions or settings. The §4.1 zero-context bar requires the doc to carry the usable setting name without requiring a reader to reconcile three competing keys against `orchestration/SKILL.md`.
